4. Royalty and revenue base

The royalty is twenty-five percent (25%) of Gross Attributable Revenue.

"Gross Attributable Revenue" means the gross revenue received by you or on
your behalf that is attributable to the licensed Software or Derivative,
including product/license sales, subscriptions, in-app purchases, advertising,
and paid services based on the Software or Derivative. It is calculated before
deducting operating costs, development costs, commissions, marketplace or
payment-processing fees, or other business expenses. Taxes separately
collected solely for remittance to a tax authority are not revenue. Actual
customer refunds reduce the corresponding revenue; a refund relating to an
already reported quarter may be credited in the next report.

If the licensed app is bundled with unrelated products or services, use a
reasonable, documented allocation based on their relative standalone value.
Unrelated business revenue is not included. You must not use a nominal or sham
allocation to avoid the royalty. The royalty is not 25% of net profit and is
not an equity interest. No minimum royalty is due for a period with zero Gross
Attributable Revenue, but a commercial licensee must still submit its report.

5. Reports, payment, and payment-channel availability

Accounting periods are calendar quarters ending March 31, June 30,
September 30, and December 31. Email a report and pay the royalty within
thirty (30) calendar days after each quarter ends, starting with the quarter
of first commercial use. Report the product/service, period, currency,
revenue categories, gross receipts, refunds/taxes excluded, any documented
bundle allocation, Gross Attributable Revenue, royalty calculation, and
payment reference. Keep records sufficient to substantiate your reports.
Amounts must be reported and paid in the same currency unless another
currency is agreed with Licensor.

Send reports and requests for payment instructions to omkasana28@gmail.com.
This email is a contact address, not a representation that it is a PayPal,
UPI, bank, or other payment account. Follow payment instructions supplied by
Licensor; do not send passwords, card details, or private banking credentials
in a report.

If no usable payment instructions have been supplied despite your timely
request, send the report and a documented offer to pay by the normal deadline
and set aside the amount due. Lack of instructions alone does not suspend
your otherwise compliant commercial permission. Pay the accrued amount within
thirty (30) calendar days after usable instructions are supplied. This is an
administrative payment arrangement, not discretionary license approval.

